--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Intended use
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

CortexSim generates controlled, high-fidelity attack-shaped signal in order to
validate that a detection stack fires as designed. It is a detection
quality-assurance engine, not a red-team command-and-control framework, and it
never writes to a Cortex tenant.

Run it ONLY against systems you own or are explicitly authorised in writing to
test. Several scenarios invoke real offensive tooling and produce telemetry
that security operations staff will treat as a genuine intrusion. Coordinate
with the owning SOC before execution.

